Long time lurker here at the r.g.r.n.. I was looking up the etymology
of labyrinth and saw how there's a connection with the root word of
labrys (a double headed axe) and labyrinth which once held the
fearsome minotaur. Most times I see minotaurs depicted in popular
culture bearing axes.

I'd like to suggest that minotaurs are generated with double headed
axes. On rare occasions have one of these monsters generated with an
artifact axe called Labrys. A player who is wielding the weapon will
only encounter peaceful minotaurs since they respect anyone who bears
this weapon. Now I did consider giving the ability to tame a minotaur
by invoking the weapon but I think that would be too powerful. By the
end game this would be largely unnecessary unless someone is pursuing
a pacifist conduct.


